        "full-cycle-03-neutral/C05_CONVEYOR_LEAD_TUNNEL.png",
        "full-cycle-03-neutral/C07_OFFICE_INTERIOR.png"
      ],
      "observation": "The large route floor stays an exceptionally uniform grey field. Subtle grain and speckled yellow markings exist, but the traffic path has very little readable finish variation or authored contact wear. The floor response remains close to a generic clean matte surface in both beauty and neutral views.",
      "repair": "Add restrained broad roughness/value variation along the approach, scanner threshold and cart movement route, with a few purposeful patches or scuffs at traffic contacts. Preserve the quiet field; avoid all-over scratches or photographic grime."
    },
    {
      "id": "M2",
      "severity": "noncritical",
      "priority": 2,
      "category": 4,
      "frames": [
        "full-cycle-03/C05_CONVEYOR_LEAD_TUNNEL.png",
        "full-cycle-03/HERO_CARGO.png",
        "full-cycle-03/HERO_UTILITIES.png",
        "full-cycle-03/HERO_EVIDENCE.png",
        "full-cycle-03-neutral/C05_CONVEYOR_LEAD_TUNNEL.png",
        "full-cycle-03-neutral/HERO_UTILITIES.png"
      ],
      "observation": "The cargo crate, large machine side panels and service/evidence doors rely heavily on their base colour and form. Most painted faces are very smooth and consistently pristine; handles, latch zones and panel lips show little local material change. This leaves a residual asset-pack finish despite useful exposed-metal highlights elsewhere.",
      "repair": "Give painted metal a restrained low-frequency roughness breakup and a small number of local contact changes at latches, handles, hinge edges and crate corners. Keep broad panel centres quiet and preserve the existing contrast with exposed conduits and matte cloth."
    },
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "severity": "minor",
      "priority": 3,
      "category": 6,
      "frames": [
        "full-cycle-03/C02_HERO_DOCK.png",
        "full-cycle-03/HERO_UTILITIES.png",
        "full-cycle-03/WALL_NORTH.png",
        "full-cycle-03-neutral/HERO_UTILITIES.png"
      ],
      "observation": "The utility cabinets and cargo machine carry brighter medium blue than the restrained dark navy architecture. This is coherent and functional, but the secondary cabinets sometimes compete with the scanner for chromatic attention.",
      "repair": "For further polish, slightly mute or darken the secondary cabinet blue while keeping the inspection machinery distinguishable. Retain the orange door/sign family and concentrated yellow hazards."
    }
  ],
